WEBVTT

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:26.560
<i>The year is 1889.</i>

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:30.980
<i>First Officer Electra tells Nadia about her past for the first time.</i>

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:34.360
<i>She says that a man destroyed her home town,</i>

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.650
<i>and her parents and little brother were killed in the destruction.</i>

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:41.490
<i>To stop Gargoyle and his Neo Atlantis organization</i>

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:44.040
<i>the Nautilus was created.</i>

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:49.540
<i>But now the Nautilus is caught in Gargoyle's trap.</i>

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:03.770
The target is in the fourth area now.

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:06.730
It's a summer insect flying into the flame of death.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:11.150
Yes. This will be your last voyage, Nautilus.

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:17.240
Two kilometers to the Kermodec Trench.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:18.740
Send out a sonar pulse.

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:19.410
Yes, Sir!

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:32.340
The enemy battleships are deployed from 2 o'clock to 10 o'clock.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:33.500
There are six of them.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:36.550
One against six. This will be tough.

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:41.260
What's worse, there must be more to our flank and beyond.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:44.060
We're in a tight pinch here.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:47.060
The target is in the third area now.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.270
Proceed to Operation D-2.

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:51.020
Yes, Sir! As you command!

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:55.150
Garfish 6 through 12, carry out the operation!

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:04.080
Torpedo tubes flooding! Distance two point two kilometers.

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:08.910
Torpedoes fired! Twenty-four of them. Distance two kilometers.

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:11.330
It's a torpedo storm.

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:15.040
Torpedoes approaching. Sixty seconds to impact.

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:16.630
Launch countermeasures.

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:17.260
Yes, Sir!

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:33.100
They've broken through the chaff curtain. Still coming!

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:35.570
All engines, top speed. Descend and evade.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:43.070
Torpedoes approaching! Twenty seconds to impact.

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:45.370
Never mind. Skim the bottom.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:50.790
They're coming!

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:58.630
Four went over us.

00:03:58.630 --> 00:03:59.630
One more left.

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:16.860
That was great, Captain!

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:19.320
We would have been destroyed if we had gone upward.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:20.990
Damage?

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:22.900
The engine is safe!

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:25.070
There's a small leak in the stern.

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:27.490
What about the Garfish?

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:30.120
Sir, six are approaching from the bow.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:32.540
Four are approaching from starboard at 2 o'clock!

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:34.960
Relative velocity is approximately eight knots!

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:38.340
Okay, let's go. First Officer!

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:43.930
Load all tubes with missiles and depth charges. Open the tubes.

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:46.260
Yes, Sir! Opening tubes.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:53.230
Fire the depth charges to the right.

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:56.400
Ten seconds later, fire the missiles at the second group!

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:57.020
Yes, Sir!

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:02.240
Depth charges are loaded.

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:04.360
Port tubes ready to fire.

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:06.700
Error correction complete.

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:07.530
Fire!

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:19.880
Missiles away.

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:35.310
Explosions confirmed. Six in number.

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:36.520
Four more left.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:42.360
Four explosions confirmed.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:45.820
We have destroyed all the Garfish we identified.

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:56.080
Ten in all. They were enthusiastic this time.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:06:00.170
First Officer, how much of our offensive weaponry is left?

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:03.340
Thirty percent left. We're loading them now.

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:07.840
Where are the other Garfish?

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:10.640
We've picked up five more, but it's strange.

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:12.930
They're leaving the area.

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:15.390
Are they going to continue the fight from a distance?

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:18.600
No, they're moving out of firing range.

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:20.560
Are they gone?

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:23.270
Not likely.

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:25.650
Be careful of attack from directly above.

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:26.150
Yes, Sir!

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:29.530
The attack will be coming from overhead.

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:36.620
The Nautilus has been found.

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:38.160
It's within our firing range.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:43.250
I'm sorry, Nemo, but you must be the subject of our experiment.

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:45.840
Carry out Operation Super Catch!

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:46.380
Yes, Sir!

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:49.010
Proceed to Phase Two.

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:51.090
Prepare the Super Catch beam gun!

00:06:57.560 --> 00:06:59.270
Tube is open.

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:00.770
Lowering the beam gun now.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:10.820
Beam gun is ready.

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:13.200
Power is being transferred.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:14.200
Magnetic field is stable.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.830
Target has been acquired.

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:17.910
Ready to fire.

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:21.370
Right. Super Catch, fire!

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:34.550
What's that?

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:37.770
The whole ship is covered with a strong magnetic field!

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:45.360
Gargoyle built a Super Catch Beam?

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:50.820
Well, Nemo, is it possible for you to get away from my new weapon?

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:57.200
The ship is being drawn upward!

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:00.000
Trim dull down! Blow the back tank!

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.040
But the ship will be inverted.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:04.880
Never mind that! Just escape from the magnetic field.

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:12.130
Prepare for heavy listing!

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:22.520
What's happening to this ship?

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:30.690
Full power to engines!

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:37.660
Useless.

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:39.490
Generating power at eighty percent.

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:57.090
It's no good! We're being dragged upward!

00:08:57.090 --> 00:08:59.930
Engine room, increase power!

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:03.310
We can't! The ship's screws won't take any more!

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:04.440
What the hell?

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:06.900
Thirty meters to surface!

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:14.570
Come on, Nautilus! Show us your entire body!

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:28.830
What's going on?

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:30.800
We're in the air.

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:37.340
A huge flying object is in the air above us!

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:42.600
What is that?

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:43.430
Incredible!

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:45.770
It's a real space battleship.

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:53.690
What's happening here?

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:56.030
Civilians aren't allowed on the bridge!

00:09:56.030 --> 00:09:58.740
Never mind all that, you silly cow.

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:02.910
We have the right to know what's going on.

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:04.040
Would you look at that?

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:05.910
We're flying in the air!

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:07.830
Is it because of that huge magnet?

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:10.170
But how is that ship flying?

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:13.960
What's that?

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:20.510
Atomic vibrator and supersonic wave gun in position.

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:22.890
We'll begin the last step of the operation.

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:25.680
It is time to test the weapon,

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:29.350
which is said to have destroyed the city of Jericho.

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:36.070
Yes. This is my invitation to Hell for you, Nemo.

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:39.820
Target will be the space titanium alloy of the Nautilus.

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:41.910
Proper pitch is set.

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:43.410
Maximum energy attained.

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:44.870
No problems in any of the systems.

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:46.000
Ready for radiation.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:47.290
Switching on!

00:10:56.880 --> 00:10:58.760
What's that sound?

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:02.180
The ship is being irradiated with concentrated electrical waves.

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:04.560
Why are they doing that?

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:19.030
The armored plating on the bow is cracking!

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:20.360
What?

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:23.320
The stern and the bottom are also cracking.

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:32.710
An atomic vibrator. Gargoyle must have built one of those too.

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:37.670
I wonder how you can stand it, Nautilus?

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:52.270
The bow's outer layer of armor has peeled off.

00:11:52.270 --> 00:11:53.850
Primary power lines are down.

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:55.730
Captain, what should we do?

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:58.190
Fire a volley. Let's fight back!

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:06.410
A barrier?

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:09.870
Our antiaircraft weapons are of no use.

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:19.420
Reserve plane lost!

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:22.010
Darn it!

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:24.340
They're going to kill us an inch at a time.

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:28.850
The third block is seriously damaged!

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:30.140
The powder magazines have been blasted!

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:33.310
The fire control system has been damaged!

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:39.570
The particle annihilation engine is straining under the load!

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:42.780
What?

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:44.240
What happened?

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:47.070
Main electric power is out!

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:49.950
This can't be...

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:51.040
It's all over.

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:57.960
The Nautilus is completely silent.

00:12:57.960 --> 00:13:00.590
Understood. Stop the attack.

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:04.260
Get me a line to the Nautilus.
I want to talk to Nemo.

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:04.930
Yes, Sir!

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:12.350
A radio message from the battleship.

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:14.560
Patch it through.

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:15.060
Yes, Sir.

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:18.520
It's been a long time, Nemo.

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:21.230
Is that you, Gargoyle?

00:13:22.940 --> 00:13:27.200
You haven't changed in thirteen years. You're still brusque.

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:29.330
It's none of your concern.

00:13:29.330 --> 00:13:33.410
Your manner will soon be gone, along with your life.

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:37.920
We never did complete our chess match.

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:40.210
Let's finish it now.

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:43.590
We don't have to. I'm the winner.

00:13:43.590 --> 00:13:47.550
You're still unyielding as well.

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:50.050
I'm sorry I can't see you again,

00:13:50.050 --> 00:13:54.020
but that's your fault since you never tried to see things my way.

00:13:54.600 --> 00:14:01.150
Now, goodbye, Nemo. Sleep forever, along with your ship.

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:09.700
Damn!

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:10.910
Isn't there anything we can do?

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:16.660
There's one way left to win.

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:19.120
We must scuttle the ship.

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:28.090
It's our only chance! Let's do it, Captain Nemo!

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:31.100
That's not just the space battleship of Neo Atlantis in front of us,

00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:32.810
but Gargoyle as well.

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:36.560
It's a golden opportunity to accomplish our purpose!

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:39.020
All we have to do is self-destruct the particle annihilation engine.

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:41.230
Then everything will be gone.

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:43.190
Let's do it, Captain Nemo!

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:47.150
We've survived thirteen years for this moment!

00:14:48.150 --> 00:14:50.240
What's the matter, Captain Nemo?

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:51.570
Please make up your mind!

00:14:54.790 --> 00:14:57.750
You used to make decisions quickly.

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:01.750
You've changed.

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:04.590
Shall I tell you the reason?

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:06.710
It's Nadia.

00:15:07.340 --> 00:15:09.880
You don't want to kill her!

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:11.390
What are you talking about?

00:15:11.390 --> 00:15:16.600
You can kill yourself if you want, but don't get others involved.

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:20.060
You must obey us as long as you are on this ship.

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:22.020
I don't think so!

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:23.360
What's that?

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:28.820
This ship's mission is to destroy Neo Atlantis even if we are killed.

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:31.280
What are you talking about, you idiot?

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:37.540
You wish to die with Captain Nemo, because you can't fulfill your love.

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:39.870
Isn't that true?

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:42.170
Oh, no! Not for me!

00:15:42.170 --> 00:15:44.130
I'll choose a way to live together.

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:50.220
I don't want to die here with you. No, thank you!

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:55.050
Let's go, everyone!

00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:59.560
Yes, Ma'am! We'll get out of here on the Gratan.

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:02.730
We don't have any reason to die here with you.

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:04.400
See you later!

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:09.110
Wait for me!

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:16.870
Don't you think the Gratan will be drawn to the huge magnet too?

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:21.370
Look! This is made of iron, but it isn't drawn to it.

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:26.340
Only the compound of the Nautilus responds to that magnet. See?

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:28.000
Oh, I see.

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:30.300
Are you really getting away?

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:34.380
Well, I said that to look good

00:16:35.050 --> 00:16:36.720
in front of Nemo.

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:42.640
I couldn't let that idiot die together with my dear Nemo.

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:43.770
Yeah!

00:16:43.770 --> 00:16:47.440
You're right! We shouldn't ever give up.

00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:51.650
That's right. It's no good to commit suicide.

00:16:51.650 --> 00:16:55.280
We must try to find a way to survive to the very end.

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:57.740
We have to find a way out?

00:16:57.740 --> 00:16:59.240
We only have one missile left.

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:02.700
Moreover, the launching tube is broken.

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:04.920
How can we make a counterattack?

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:09.960
Yes, the question is how to get out of this pinch.

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:11.920
Yes, that's it!

00:17:12.630 --> 00:17:14.340
There's a way.

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:19.050
I'm sure they'll open one of the large tubes for the finishing blow.

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:22.270
The barrier will be lowered at that time.

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:25.560
We fire into it at that instant.

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:28.060
It will explode inside.

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:32.030
Yes. It's the only way to make a counterattack.

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:35.860
Don't be absurd! We don't even know where the tube is!

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:37.320
I think we must

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:39.410
try it before we give up.

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:43.370
We must believe in its probability.

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:45.330
Manually?

00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:49.380
Yes, open the tube manually.

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:51.590
See to it right away.

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:52.670
Yes, Sir!

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:55.800
Who is going to aim it at the battleship's tube?

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:58.340
Leave it to us!

00:18:01.640 --> 00:18:03.600
We'll get out of here on the Gratan.

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:06.310
Please take the chance to make a counterattack.

00:18:08.850 --> 00:18:11.110
Take care, Captain Nemo.

00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:14.070
Good luck.

00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:16.450
Well, let's go!

00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:18.530
But before that...

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:26.120
Let me go with you!

00:18:26.790 --> 00:18:28.000
No way!

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:29.290
Why not?

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:34.420
You must watch over Nadia, Marie and King. That's a man's duty.

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:35.880
But...

00:18:36.130 --> 00:18:39.840
Listen, Jean. It's important to protect others,

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:42.550
but you have to protect your own life too.

00:18:43.600 --> 00:18:45.020
You must survive!

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:47.850
Yes, you, too.

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:51.190
Of course. Good luck!

00:18:55.440 --> 00:18:58.360
Our life is such a checkered one, isn't it?

00:18:58.360 --> 00:19:00.360
Yeah, we never get bored.

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:02.490
As long as we survive.

00:19:02.990 --> 00:19:04.410
Let's go!

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:05.740
Okay!

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:07.950
What's happening?

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:10.750
It's concentrated fire from the Garfish.

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:19.880
Damn! The space battleship won't open its tubes in this situation.

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:23.300
Without electricity, this hatch doesn't open!

00:19:23.300 --> 00:19:25.680
Never mind that! Blast it off!

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:26.600
Check!

00:19:29.980 --> 00:19:32.730
Change to flight mode!

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:34.150
Switch on!

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:49.450
The tectite net is spread. It will hold for a while.

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:50.870
All right then!

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:56.590
Sorry. That's the last techno bomb left.

00:19:56.590 --> 00:19:57.880
Good luck, Sanson!

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:01.340
Leave it to me! I'm a genius with a gun!

00:20:06.720 --> 00:20:10.310
It's very good for shooting practice.

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:13.480
The rate of hits is pretty low.

00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:15.230
I'm sorry, Sir!

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:16.270
Wind speed?

00:20:16.270 --> 00:20:17.110
Six meters!

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:17.940
Temperature?

00:20:17.940 --> 00:20:19.190
22 degrees centigrade!

00:20:19.190 --> 00:20:20.110
Air pressure?

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:21.070
Point ninety-four!

00:20:21.070 --> 00:20:21.820
Distance?

00:20:21.820 --> 00:20:23.110
One point two kilometers!

00:20:23.610 --> 00:20:26.580
Why didn't you put the tectite over the cabin?

00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:28.410
I had no time!

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:29.580
Stupid!

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:32.540
Open it quickly! I'll blast it off with a single shot!

00:20:32.910 --> 00:20:34.500
Let's go!

00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:37.960
Heave ho!

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:41.420
It seems we depend upon this ship's machinery too much.

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:44.890
I think so too. This is what happens when the power is cut.

00:20:51.850 --> 00:20:53.940
Second vertical engine damaged!

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:56.020
No answer from the starboard quarters!

00:20:56.020 --> 00:20:57.440
How about the factory area?

00:20:57.440 --> 00:21:00.900
We don't know! It may be destroyed.

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:05.950
Nadia!

00:21:08.780 --> 00:21:10.290
Please! Stop it!

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:14.250
I'll give you the Blue Water! Just stop killing each other!

00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:17.830
Lord Gargoyle, it's Nadia!

00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:21.170
I see. I thought she might be on the Nautilus.

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:22.800
What shall we do?

00:21:24.170 --> 00:21:28.760
Interesting. She is still useful. Bring her here.

00:21:35.060 --> 00:21:35.770
Nadia!

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:37.520
Jean!

00:21:39.690 --> 00:21:41.110
Nadia!

00:21:41.690 --> 00:21:42.980
That's it!

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:45.200
We have captured Nadia.

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:48.240
I see. It's checkmate now.

00:21:48.240 --> 00:21:51.410
Yes, Sir! Prepare the annihilation bomb.

00:21:51.410 --> 00:21:58.120
We'll look for Nemo's Blue Water later with the help of the Emperor.

00:22:03.760 --> 00:22:04.630
Is that it?

00:22:18.520 --> 00:22:19.690
The bow is destroyed!

00:22:19.690 --> 00:22:23.480
Damn! We'll be finished if we get one more of those!

00:22:26.360 --> 00:22:28.780
They've loaded the bomb already.

00:22:28.780 --> 00:22:30.910
Can't you hold it steady?

00:22:30.910 --> 00:22:32.870
Heave ho!

00:22:34.410 --> 00:22:35.330
There!

00:22:35.620 --> 00:22:38.580
Right! The next time is my chance!

00:22:40.460 --> 00:22:42.420
It'll be a miracle if we can nail it!

00:22:42.420 --> 00:22:43.590
We must perform

00:22:44.050 --> 00:22:46.050
this miracle by ourselves!

00:22:49.130 --> 00:22:50.300
You did it!

00:22:58.310 --> 00:23:02.270
Someone help us!

00:23:02.650 --> 00:23:03.860
Darn it!

00:23:06.900 --> 00:23:07.860
Go!

00:23:15.700 --> 00:23:17.120
Nice landing!

00:23:19.580 --> 00:23:20.960
Now! Fire!

00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:32.260
We did it! The magnetic force is weakening!

00:23:35.720 --> 00:23:38.430
We're falling! Brace for impact!

00:23:45.860 --> 00:23:47.400
How did this happen?

00:23:47.400 --> 00:23:49.280
I'm sorry, Sir!

00:23:49.280 --> 00:23:54.490
Never mind. I'll discuss your punishment later.

00:23:54.490 --> 00:23:55.370
Yes, Sir!

00:23:55.370 --> 00:23:59.080
The Nautilus won't last long.

00:23:59.080 --> 00:24:01.330
Deliver the final blow with the Garfish.

00:24:01.330 --> 00:24:02.540
Yes, Sir!

00:24:02.540 --> 00:24:05.040
The Nautilus is sinking.

00:24:11.880 --> 00:24:14.300
That is the fate of fools.
